    "background_story": "Ahmad was a brilliant and eccentric marine biologist who spent his life studying the mysterious synentognathi, a group of ancient, deep-sea fish with fused jaws. Growing up in a coastal town, Ahmad was fascinated by the ocean's unknown regions and spent countless hours exploring the tide pools and coral reefs near his home. As he delved deeper into his research, Ahmad became obsessed with uncovering the secrets of the synentognathi, which were thought to have remained unchanged for millions of years. His groundbreaking research took him to the depths of the Mariana Trench, where he discovered new species and shed light on the evolution of these enigmatic creatures. Ahmad's work sparked a new wave of interest in deep-sea exploration and earned him the nickname 'The Synentognathi Whisperer' among his peers.",
